 "notes": "Names: the street I call Badgly Avenue is printed W BADGLY S AVE. north of Tarrant Street (W. Badgly's Avenue?) and BADGLY ... AVE. south of Kentucky Avenue; same alignment, interrupted by the McClure tract. Carlin Street likewise appears in three pieces on one alignment (label CARLIN / ST.). The 46 ft avenue running north-north-east from Chase Avenue to Kirby Avenue carries only AVE. north of the bend; I take it as Virginia Avenue continuing (VIRGINIA is printed south-west of Chase). Chase Avenue: the east-west Chase Avenue meets Virginia at 1456,4640, and the diagonal piece labelled CHASE AVE. (50 ft) leaves Virginia at 1313,4752 to the north-west and continues as LEHER ST. (30 ft, reading uncertain). ? at 2097,1323 and 2746,1322: 25 ft street along the top neat line, only ST. printed. ? at 1428,1537: unnamed 30 ft street. Virginia/Kirby: Virginia peels off Kirby just south of that top street, a long acute junction with the wedge tip near 2690,1555. Martha/Carlin: Martha Street merges into Carlin at an acute angle around a small triangular island (1305-1345, 1650-1740); the point given is where the centrelines meet, the open plaza centre is nearer 1300,1720. Schneider: suffix not read (label runs off my strip). ? at 659,5194: a road stub entering Colerain from the west plate edge, printed RD. only. Kentucky/Leeper: north of Kentucky the same road is printed QUARRY STREET, south of it LEEPER AVE.; the road is partly cut by the plate edge. Sagateo Alley: reading of the name uncertain. HANIFIELD is the printed spelling. Kirby Avenue south of Chase is read from the KIRBY label just north of Chase at x 2830; Kirby x Chase is near 2800,4952 (outside x 2700, not recorded). Unnamed alleys not recorded: 20 ft alley north of Robley at x 2145; 20 ft alleys at 880-930,3860-4030 and 1290-1440,4170-4480; 12 ft alleys round the block between Jerome and Georgia south of Chase. Martha Street suffix not printed in my strip (assumed Street). | Names: the west-edge street is printed QUARRY ... STREET north of about y 2700 and LEEPER ... AVE. from Colerain Avenue up to Kentucky Avenue; I used Leeper Avenue at Kentucky. The avenue with 43xx/42xx house numbers from the Kirby fork (2697,1540) down to Chase is labelled only AVE.; I call it Virginia Avenue because it runs straight into the street printed VIRGINIA south-west of Chase and the house numbers continue. Kirby Avenue (60 ft) continues south-south-east from the fork, off this strip, and comes back as the street printed KI... at x about 2770 on Chase, crossing Hanifield at (2668,5613). N BADGLY (no suffix printed) south of Tarrant lines up with the avenue labelled AVE. north of Tarrant, recorded as one street, North Badgly Avenue; the same line reappears as the Badgly Avenue stub north of Kentucky (printed BADGLY south of Washburn). The street along y 1325 (25 ft, then a 30 ft diagonal to Martha) has only ST. printed in this strip: '?'. Georgia and Florida are printed without a clear suffix south of Chase (a T and an S of ST. are visible) and their legs north of Chase are labelled only AVE.; Florida's northern leg runs to Bruce Avenue and is recorded as Florida Avenue there. Leher Street (30 ft) widens and continues as Chase Avenue (50 ft) at (775,4243). Chase Avenue is offset at Virginia Avenue: the north-west leg meets it at (1323,4743), the east leg at (1445,4650). The road leaving Colerain Avenue to the west at (664,5212) has only RD. on the plate. Lambston is my reading of the label (LAMBSTON), about 20 ft wide. Agate Alley is my reading of the short alley between Hemlock and Cypress Alleys. Block 62 (Jerome to Georgia) has unnamed 12 ft alleys, not picked. Lines marked 12' W. and 18' W. between Leher Street, Lambston and the foot of Carlin look like private ways, not picked. Chase x Kirby (x about 2775) is past the 2700 limit and not picked."
